    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d403">

                <pb facs="0361" n="287" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg287"/>

                <head>Mr. Hunter to Mr. Bigelow</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 128]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-05-05"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 5, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your very interesting despatch, of the 18th
                    ultimo, in regard to the effect produced by the news of the flight of Lee and
                    the fall of Petersburg and Richmond, and giving translations of the comments of
                    the leading French journals upon the events, has been received.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. HUNTER, <hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                    Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Bigelow,</hi> Esq., <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >&amp;c.,&amp;c.,&amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
